simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.1=This machine has two modes: single step and parallel timeline
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.2=Both modes overclock without loss, and both reach 2147483647 parallels
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.3=Single step:
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.4=Consumes the reagents and produces the product in one step by manipulating atoms
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.5=Parallel timeline:
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.6=Unlocked while the space time continuum ripper blocks are present
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.7=It tears spacetime open over and over and pulls the reagents out of a parallel timeline
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.8=In this mode it consumes no reagents at all
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.9=Supports multi-amp energy hatches and laser hatches
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.10=Can take its power straight out of the wireless network (switch on the right of the GUI)
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.11=Every hatch - energy, maintenance, input hatch, output hatch, input bus, output bus - goes on a Chemically Inert Machine Casing
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.12=The input bus positions also take the pattern provider and the ME input bus; the output bus positions also take the ME output bus
simplification.tooltip.molecularPolymerFabricator.13=Mod: GT Simplification  Contributors: Tangent95, QionSi

